<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow prose">
    <p>What that's meant in practice: a showroom grown to more than seventy-five designer lines. A floor merchandised so you can actually see how light behaves instead of squinting at a catalog. A free lighting consultation that walks a homeowner through every fixture in the house. Relationships with dozens of the builders working around Bryan–College Station. And a team that can do all of it without her in the building — which is the part she's proudest of and the part nobody notices.</p>
    <blockquote class="quote">
      <p>“I like the moment somebody stops being overwhelmed. They come in with a folder and a number and this look on their face, and an hour later they're pointing at things going ‘that one, in the entry.’ That's the whole job. Everything else is just knowing the lines.”</p>
      <footer>Becca Keefauver, Owner</footer>
    </blockquote>

    <h2>How this started</h2>
    <p>A friend from church approached Jeff about buying his lighting showroom. George McCoy heard about it, got excited, and wanted in. Becca was the natural person to lead the new store — she's run it ever since, and built it into what it is today.</p>
    <p>That's it. It's not a business story, it's a College Station story: somebody you know from church has a business, a friend gets excited, and it turns out your wife is the one who can run it.</p>
    <p>Aggieland Lighting and Design is owned by two local families — Becca and Jeff Keefauver, and George and Amie McCoy.</p>
  </div>
</section>

